{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-07T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On 8 August, curiosity takes centre stage on International Infinity Day—a celebration inspired by the sideways figure 8, a symbol of something without end. Founded in 1987 by New York–based philosopher Jean-Pierre Ady Fenyo, the date (8/8) was chosen because the number 8, when turned on its side, becomes the infinity symbol, or lemniscate, first introduced by English mathematician John Wallis in 1655. The day celebrates philosophy, science, art and the endless possibilities of human imagination.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_EN-GB3847788744_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_EN-GB3847788744_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Crossing into infinity","Title":"Infinity Bridge in Stockton-on-Tees, England","Copyright":"© Bahadir Yeniceri/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.5647944,-1.2991917/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.5647944,-1.2991917;S9;Infinity Bridge, Stockton-on-Tees, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260808_StocktonInfinity\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Infinity+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260807_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260808_StocktonInfinity"},"Ssd":"20260808","Name":"StocktonInfinity","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3847788744","FullDateString":"8 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"It all started with an idea shared over a pint. Today, that conversation has grown into Europe's largest annual hot air balloon festival. Every summer, the Bristol International Balloon Fiesta fills the skies above Ashton Court Estate with more than 100 colourful balloons, attracting over half a million visitors.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BristolBalloonFiesta2026_EN-GB3752871643_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BristolBalloonFiesta2026_EN-GB3752871643_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Up, up and hooray!","Title":"Hot air balloons above Bristol city centre, England","Copyright":"© Rich Jones Photography/Moment/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.453133,-2.600982/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.453133,-2.600982;S9;Bristol, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260807_BristolBalloonFiesta2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bristol+International+Balloon+Fiesta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260806_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260807_BristolBalloonFiesta2026"},"Ssd":"20260807","Name":"BristolBalloonFiesta2026","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3752871643","FullDateString":"7 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In the Masai Mara, Kenya, the ground seems to move. A vast surge of wildebeest—hoofed grazers built for endurance—travel s in tightly packed herds, drawn by fresh grass and water replenished by seasonal rains.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_EN-GB8480696688_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaraCrossing_EN-GB8480696688_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where the river tests the brave","Title":"Migrating wildebeest crossing Mara River in Masai Mara, Kenya","Copyright":"© Manoj Shah/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Weighing as much as 275 kilograms, adult wildebeests rank among the larger herbivorous antelope species.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildebeest&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260805_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260806_MaraCrossing"},"Ssd":"20260806","Name":"MaraCrossing","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"8480696688","FullDateString":"6 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Fez, Morocco, the Royal Palace—known as Dar al-Makhzen—has stood as a seat of power since the 13th century, when Morocco's rulers established a fortified royal city around it. Behind its high walls lie gardens, courtyards, mosques and royal residences spread across a vast complex still used by the king today, making it both historic and fully active.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FezMorocco_EN-GB7904978053_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FezMorocco_EN-GB7904978053_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Gates of a hidden kingdom","Title":"Decorated gate of the Royal Palace of Fez, Morocco","Copyright":"© cgst26/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.05306,-4.99361/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.05306,-4.99361;S9;Fez, Morocco&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260805_FezMorocco\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Royal+Palace+of+Fez&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260804_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260805_FezMorocco"},"Ssd":"20260805","Name":"FezMorocco","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7904978053","FullDateString":"5 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Owls take centre stage on International Owl Awareness Day, an annual observance highlighting their remarkable adaptations and worldwide distribution. Found on every continent except Antarctica, these birds are known for forward-facing eyes, flat facial discs that channel sound and specialised hearing. Many species hunt in near silence thanks to soft-edged feathers. Their eyes remain fixed in their sockets, so they rely on flexible necks to scan their surroundings. From forests to deserts, owls inhabit a wide range of environments and play an important role in maintaining ecosystem balance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AdorableOwlet_EN-GB7610468145_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AdorableOwlet_EN-GB7610468145_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hoot hoot hooray!","Title":"Florida burrowing owlet, Cape Coral, Florida, United States","Copyright":"© mlorenzphotography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Owls can rotate their heads up to 270° to compensate for eyes that are fixed in their sockets.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260804_AdorableOwlet\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Owl+bird&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260803_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260804_AdorableOwlet"},"Ssd":"20260804","Name":"AdorableOwlet","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7610468145","FullDateString":"4 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Colourful luzzus—traditional Maltese fishing boats—fill the sheltered harbour of Marsaxlokk, a village on Malta's southeastern coast. Just a short drive from Valletta, the island's capital, it remains one of the country's main fishing hubs, where daily life follows the steady pace of the sea. Home to roughly 4,000 residents, the village is also widely known for its lively waterfront, especially its popular Sunday fish market and for the steady return of boats carrying fresh catches each morning.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BoatsMalta_EN-GB7267750671_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BoatsMalta_EN-GB7267750671_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Bright boats, timeless traditions","Title":"Colourful boats in Marsaxlokk Harbour, Malta","Copyright":"© Klubovy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.842987,14.54532/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.842987,14.54532;S9;Marsaxlokk, Malta&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260803_BoatsMalta\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Marsaxlokk+Malta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260802_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260803_BoatsMalta"},"Ssd":"20260803","Name":"BoatsMalta","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7267750671","FullDateString":"3 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Finland is famous for the northern lights, its high happiness rankings, saunas and thousands of lakes. Helsinki adds history, design and the Baltic Sea to that list. The story begins in 1550, when King Gustav I of Sweden founded a trading town that would become Finland's capital in 1812. Today, a walk through the city can take you from Senate Square and the white-domed Helsinki Cathedral to the sea fortress of Suomenlinna, a UNESCO World Heritage Site accessible by ferry.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HelsinkiBlue_EN-GB6980168660_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HelsinkiBlue_EN-GB6980168660_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Daughter of the Baltic","Title":"Helsinki's shoreline during blue hour, Uusimaa, Finland","Copyright":"© Miemo Penttinen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/60.208715,25.004253/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=60.208715,25.004253;S9;Helsinki, Uusimaa, Finland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260802_HelsinkiBlue\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Helsinki&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260801_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260802_HelsinkiBlue"},"Ssd":"20260802","Name":"HelsinkiBlue","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6980168660","FullDateString":"2 Aug 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Nature has a knack for balancing the impossible. In New Mexico's Ah-Shi-Sle-Pah Wilderness in the United States, towering hoodoos perch hefty rock caps on slender stems. Wind, water and ice have spent roughly 75 million years sculpting these remote badlands into an open-air gallery that feels more alien than terrestrial.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_EN-GB5755022749_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ValleyDreams_EN-GB5755022749_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The great balancing act","Title":"Hoodoos in Ah‑Shi‑Sle‑Pah Wilderness in San Juan County, New Mexico, United States","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.155291,-107.935427/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.155291,-107.935427;S9;Ah‑Shi‑Sle‑Pah Wilderness, New Mexico, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260815_ValleyDreams\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ah+Shi+Sle+Pah+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260814_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260815_ValleyDreams"},"Ssd":"20260815","Name":"ValleyDreams","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5755022749","FullDateString":"15 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Roads solved one problem but quietly created another. People could travel faster than ever, while wildlife now faced highways cutting across routes they had followed for generations. The result was more collisions, fragmented habitats and isolated wildlife populations. That challenge led to building wildlife crossings called ecoducts: bridges or tunnels designed to reconnect habitats and give animals a safe way across busy roads. Some of the earliest modern examples appeared in France during the 1950s, while countries such as the Netherlands refined the concept with broad, vegetation-covered bridges that blend into the surrounding landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_EN-GB5514216597_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_EN-GB5514216597_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Built for paws, not people","Title":"Aerial view of a wildlife crossing near Zakrzów, Poland","Copyright":"© bbsferrari/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In 1950s France, the first wildlife crossings took shape, offering animals a way through landscapes newly divided by roads.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260814_WildlifeCrossingPoland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildlife+crossing&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260813_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260814_WildlifeCrossingPoland"},"Ssd":"20260814","Name":"WildlifeCrossingPoland","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5514216597","FullDateString":"14 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Not every summer tradition happens on the ground. Some take place hundreds of miles overhead, one meteor at a time. The Perseids return every year from mid-July through late August, reaching their peak around 12-13 August. Visible across much of the world, they often produce dozens of meteors per hour under dark skies. Picture yourself looking up. One streak appears after another. How many can you spot before you lose count? Each streak comes from debris shed by Comet Swift-Tuttle as Earth moves through its dust trail. The meteors appear to radiate from the constellation Perseus.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_EN-GB6939134267_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_EN-GB6939134267_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Make a wish","Title":"Perseid meteors over Teide Observatory, Tenerife, Spain","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/28.291565,-16.629129/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=28.291565,-16.629129;S9;Teide Observatory, Tenerife, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Perseids+meteor+shower&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260812_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife"},"Ssd":"20260813","Name":"PerseidasTenerife","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6939134267","FullDateString":"13 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On 12 August, World Elephant Day invites us to pause and consider not just the size of these animals, but the depth of their lives. In places like Amboseli National Park in Kenya—captured in this image—a herd doesn't simply pass through the landscape; it remembers it. Matriarchs guide their families between water sources, tracing routes shaped as much by memory as by terrain.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_EN-GB4622751774_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_EN-GB4622751774_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Giants worth protecting","Title":"A group of elephants, Amboseli National Park, Kenya","Copyright":"© Ibrahim Suha Derbent/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-2.6527,37.26058/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-2.6527,37.26058;S9;Amboseli National Park, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Elephant+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260811_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay"},"Ssd":"20260812","Name":"ElephantDay","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"4622751774","FullDateString":"12 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Copenhagen, Nyhavn Canal is a burst of colour and history. In Denmark's capital, bright, gabled houses lean towards the water, their reflections rippling beside old wooden ships.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_EN-GB4254714055_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ColorfulCop_EN-GB4254714055_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Copenhagen in full colour","Title":"Colourful homes line Nyhavn Canal, Copenhagen, Denmark","Copyright":"© emicristea/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/55.680387,12.589468/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=55.680387,12.589468;S9;Nyhavn, Copenhagen, Denmark&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260811_ColorfulCop\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Nyhavn+Canal+Copenhagen&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260810_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260811_ColorfulCop"},"Ssd":"20260811","Name":"ColorfulCop","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"4254714055","FullDateString":"11 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Where two great deserts meet, Joshua Tree National Park reveals a stark, mesmerising landscape shaped by wind, time and extremes. In Southern California, United States, the higher Mojave Desert merges with the hotter, lower Colorado Desert, creating a unique blend of ecosystems and remarkable biodiversity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_EN-GB4047990489_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_EN-GB4047990489_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where two deserts collide","Title":"Joshua Tree National Park, California, United States","Copyright":"© JJ Landscapes/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/33.951965,-115.942135/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=33.951965,-115.942135;S9;Joshua Tree National Park, California, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260810_SandPath\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Joshua+Tree+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260809_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260810_SandPath"},"Ssd":"20260810","Name":"SandPath","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"4047990489","FullDateString":"10 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, the International Day of the World's Indigenous Peoples invites a closer look at communities whose stories stretch far beyond recorded history. Proclaimed by the United Nations in 1994 and first observed in 1995, the date marks a landmark 1982 meeting focused on protecting Indigenous rights worldwide. More than 476 million Indigenous people now live across about 90 countries, sustaining thousands of cultures and the majority of the world's roughly 7,000 languages.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_EN-GB3964962434_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JMTjibaou_EN-GB3964962434_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Architecture of identity","Title":"Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, New Caledonia","Copyright":"© Fabien Astre/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-22.256,166.482/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-22.256,166.482;S9;Jean-Marie Tjibaou Cultural Centre, New Caledonia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260809_JMTjibaou\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Day+of+the+W